+Active identity (2026-10-13) is defined once in `validation_common.py`: SDK
+`317422076650`; ASIC `327743061057`; firmware-update ID `327743061057`;
+USB descriptor serial `327743061057`, separately observed. Historical SDK
+`243322073847` and ASIC/USB `251843061466` remain in archived evidence.
+Expected firmware `5.17.3.10`; BMI085 must be read and verified by N1, since
+the new-unit snapshot omitted IMU type. No firmware update is part of a mismatch
 response. N1 receipts expire after two hours or reboot and seal raw evidence.
+The preparation `n3_baseline.yaml` is a serial template. Bundle construction
+resolves it into a native parameter file; `n3_record.py` also writes and seals
+its resolved session copy before launch. Do not pass the unresolved template
+directly to ROS. The permission inventory helper now imports the adjacent
+`validation_common.py`; do not deploy it alone using historical install commands.
+The archived `99-wbr-d435i.rules` still targets the old descriptor serial and
+is retained unchanged; this ticket does not install or apply permission files.
+
+### Explicit latched-power diagnosis (OPEN only)
+
+Strict mode still requires `throttled=0x0`. If the user explicitly chooses to
+continue with latched history, add `--diagnostic-latched-power` to N1 and to
+**each** `phase_gate.py n2` command below. Camera authorization is still required.
+Only bits 16-19 (`0xF0000`) may be set: `0x50000` is allowed for diagnosis,
+while any live bit 0-3 or any unknown bit stops the run. Health monitoring uses
+the same mask, and new kernel/SDK power faults still stop the run.
+
+Every N1/N2 result records `power_mode` and raw throttling; N2 also preserves
+all raw one-Hz power samples. If failure precedes a power observation, the raw
+field is null rather than invented. Successful diagnostic N1/N2 runs exit zero
+for deliberate stage progression but have verdict **OPEN_DIAGNOSTIC**, even if
+the observed value is zero. They never establish hardware PASS. Without the
+flag, diagnostic receipts cannot enter N2; `accept-n2` refuses diagnostic
+N1 or capture inputs. N3 remains blocked by its strict N2 PASS prerequisite.
+The exact raw profile, timing bands and mandatory 300-second soak are unchanged.
 
 ## Future N2 stages
 
